In the past three years, there has been a significant increase in research on fairness-aware data publication selection for recommender systems. This paper presents an approach to address this issue by introducing a novel framework called FairCoverage that allows users to specify their desired level of demographic coverage and similarity requirements when querying for recommendations. The system then provides a set of results that satisfy these criteria, ensuring fairness in the selection process.

The paper presents an algorithmic solution to achieve data coverage while maintaining fairness constraints on sensitive attributes such as gender or race. It also introduces a novel approach called FairCoverage which allows users to specify their desired level of demographic (sub)group coverage and similarity requirements when querying for recommendations, ensuring that the system provides results within these specified ranges in a responsible manner [39].

